# Settings

- Shared values in `base.py`; only differences in `development` / `test` /
  `production`. No fourth settings module, no `config/` package.
- Every environment-dependent value is read through `core/settings/env.py`
  (`get_bool` / `get_int` / `get_list` / `build_mailer`) and documented in
  `.env.example`. No secret literals.
- `test.py` stays hermetic: anything `.env` can change must be pinned there.
- `production.py` keeps its fail-fast guards (secret key, allowed hosts) and
  the secure cookie / HSTS / WhiteNoise block.
- Email uses `MAILERS` (Django 6.1); `EMAIL_*` is deprecated and removed in 7.0.
- Adding a setting means updating `.env.example` and, when behaviour depends on
  it, a test in `tests/test_settings.py`.

See skills: `starter-architecture`, `django-logging`, `django-caching`.
